< https://github.com/tacplus-dev/tacplus/issues/314#issuecomment-7153692777
This run did not get the fix queued. The code is ready and passed the pre-land gate, but a looper bug stopped both `--land` and `--checkpoint` before they could push.

- **Pre-land gate passed.** I recommitted the work unchanged as 850014c3 (code) and 9cf93b60 (STATE.md), on main aae6eb5, which hasn't moved. The tree is identical to the last queued version (93ce71ee). The pre-land gate passed this time in about 18 minutes (pipeline 3111843425). `just test` also passes locally in 6m37s.
- **The earlier send-backs were build-side.** Three pre-land builds were cancelled and one lost its runner or timed out, against a 5-minute budget. None reported a test failure. I posted that on the issue for the hub (comment 7153078676) before landing again.
- **Nothing was pushed or queued.** The tool's lock step fails with `Permission denied` on `/builds/looper/tacplus/.checkpoint.1728249028.lock`. Setup pre-creates only `.checkpoint.lock` for this run's user, while the checkpoint locks a per-checkout file this user can't create in the root-owned work directory. Working around it would mean moving every path the tool uses, so I left it alone. I reported the bug on the issue for the hub, with the line numbers in `repo-looper` (comment 7153692777).

**Left for the next run:**
1. Push the two commits. The looper's own checkpoint when this run stops should do that.
2. Run `--land`. No code change is needed, but if the lock bug isn't fixed by then, it will fail the same way.
3. After the manager's verdict: post the outcome comment (commits, gates, gate set and batch) and close #314.

Nothing has run on Windows yet; that leg is #490. There is no patch tag, since Jody decided this ships in 2.7 only.
